# CLI Documentation Closure — Era Implementation Status

A per-era rollup across the ~47-version roadmap (`00-architecture.docs`). Summary/index
only — each era's `.docs` file carries its own per-version Goal/Reuses/Implement/Validate/
Done-when, and `gaps/00-index.docs` carries the open questions found during audit.

Legend: ✅ done · 🟡 in progress · ⬜ not started · ⚠️ partial · ⛔ blocked

**Overall: ✅ All four phases done, verified 2026-09-17 · re-verified 2026-09-17. Phase 1
(Eras 1–2): ground truth and templates — re-verification found and fixed 3 real extraction
bugs (`gaps/011`) and a stale flag-count figure (`gaps/009`). Phase 2 (Eras 3–11): every
family reference page published — re-verification (a systematic per-family flag-coverage
cross-check, all 54 groups) found and closed 2 planning omissions (`environment`, `project`
never assigned to any era) plus a third unassigned group (`speccmd`, now `cli/spec.mdx`),
rewrote 3 pre-existing stub pages that predated this roadmap and were never actually
completed despite "documented" status (`environment.mdx`, `project.mdx`, `init.mdx`), and
added missing flags to 5 otherwise-substantial pages (`config`, `alie`, `edge`, `firewall`,
`container`) — full account in `gaps/012`. Phase 3 (Era 12): four task guides published, nav
wired, every Era 1 naming ambiguity traced to its resolution — `gaps/003` (`plan`/`plans`)
now fully resolved rather than deferred: both are real, current commands, confirmed via
source. Phase 4 (Era 13): every example marked verified-or-reviewed, a full-repo disclosure
sweep found zero leaks — re-swept 2026-09-17 across every page changed in re-verification,
same result. The per-change gate lives in `beaver-cli/CLAUDE.md`, the periodic-refresh
cadence is recorded in `00-architecture.docs` (the per-family flag-coverage cross-check used
in this re-verification is now the recommended first step of that cadence, per `gaps/012`).
`mint broken-links` clean throughout.**

Repo: `mintlify` (this repo — the docs site). Source of truth audited: `beaver-cli`
(`~/Desktop/vhb/beaver-cli`, `commands/`, 458 Go files, ~65 top-level groups). Backend
(`~/Desktop/works/vhb-server`) is referenced only if a command's behavior needs server-side
confirmation (mirrors how `features/cloud/eras_implementation.docs` in `beaver-desktop`
flags "the code wins" over stale docs) — not otherwise in scope.

---

## Pre-work already captured (folds into Era 1)

A first-pass census was run against `beaver-cli/commands/` while scoping this roadmap:

- Full `Use:` extraction across all 458 Go files (415 command definitions found).
- Per-group flag-definition site counts (proxy for doc effort): `machine` 60, `config` 55,
  `alie` 53, `edge` 42, `firewall` 41, `service` 37, `cloud` 34, `deploy` 32, `scaling` 24,
  `compose` 24, and a long tail down to single-digit groups.
- Diff of `beaver-cli/commands/*` directories against `cli/*.mdx` basenames: 28 command
  groups have **no** matching doc page (`admin`, `auth`, `autoscale`, `cloud`, `config`,
  `coupon`, `deployui`, `envbanner`, `health`, `initcmd`, `integration`, `internal`,
  `mcpcmd`, `mystic`, `observability`, `preflight`, `projectconfig`, `projectcontext`,
  `projectcontract`, `promote`, `reconcilecmd`, `route`, `service`, `skillscmd`, `speccmd`,
  `state`, `statecmd`, `ui`); 15 existing doc pages have no matching top-level command
  directory (`containers`, `contract`, `init`, `integrations`, `login`, `logout`, `logs`,
  `metrics`, `plan`, `plans`, `shell`, `traffic`, `validate`, `version`, `whoami`) — several
  of these are legitimate (they map to a subcommand of an undocumented parent, e.g.
  `logs`/`metrics`/`traffic` → `observability`; `login`/`logout`/`whoami` → `auth`), others
  may be stale (`plan`/`plans` predate the current model per `CLAUDE.md`).
- Full subcommand listing pulled for the two largest zero-coverage groups: `service` (37
  distinct `Use:` strings across `service`, `database`, `cluster`, `backup-destination`
  subgroups) and `cloud` (29 distinct `Use:` strings).
- `statecmd` (`apply`/`drift`/`history`/`pull`/`rollback`/`status`) and `projectcontract`
  (`plan`/`diff`/`push`/`pull`/`rollback`/`status`/`validate`/`containers`/`delete`) flagged
  as the highest disclosure-risk families — their vocabulary (drift, reconcile, contract,
  plan) is adjacent to the internal deployment-contract schema `CLAUDE.md` names as a trade
  secret.

**This pre-work does not replace Era 1** — V1–V4 formalize it into the checked-in,
row-per-command inventory this roadmap is graded against, including flag-level detail (not
just subcommand names) and a maturity classification per row (implemented-usable /
available-but-limited / placeholder-unfinished / documented-but-stale).

---

## Phase 1 — Ground truth

### Era 1 — Command Inventory & Audit (V1–V4) — ✅ done, verified 2026-09-17 · **GATING**

Built as real, checked-in artifacts under `inventory/`, not just prose:

- **V1** `extract_commands.py` — parses every `.go` file under `beaver-cli/commands/` for
  literal `&cobra.Command{}` definitions (Pass A) and factory-function-generated commands
  (Pass B: `return &cobra.Command{}` inside a helper, resolved package-wide since Go files in
  one directory share a package; Pass C: commands passed inline into `AddCommand()` with no
  variable). Flags are attributed by matching each `<var>.Flags().XVar(...)` call's receiver
  variable back to the command it was declared against — the actual pattern this codebase
  uses (flags registered in a bottom-of-file `init()`, not nested in the literal). Iterated
  four times against real bugs found by spot-checking (Validate's own instruction): an
  attribution bug that put a different command's flags on the wrong page, a regex that
  silently dropped every other line in a multi-command `var (...)` block, and two rounds of
  cross-file/inline factory-call resolution. Final spot-check against the 5 named groups
  (service, cloud, config, machine, alie) matched independent manual greps closely.
  **439 distinct commands, 481 flags, 53 real command-group directories.**
  **Re-verified 2026-09-17** (per-era status headers had drifted out of sync with these
  artifacts — see `01-command-inventory-and-audit.docs`'s own note): a repeat of this same
  spot-check found 3 more real extraction bugs — anonymous inline command literals
  (`config init`/`config sync`), two root-level commands entirely outside `commands/`
  (`beaver shell`, `beaver destroy` — the latter destructive and completely undocumented),
  and systematically off source line numbers. All fixed in `extract_commands.py`; pipeline
  re-run end to end. **Now 443 distinct commands, 54 real command-group directories.** Full
  account in `gaps/00-index.docs` entry 011.
- **V2** `cross_reference.py` — diffs command groups against `cli/*.mdx`, applying the
  manual mapping worked out for the 15 orphaned pages found in scoping (observability
  subcommands, auth subcommands, etc.). Output: `doc_status.csv`.
- **V3** maturity pass folded into `build_summary.py` — checked for `Hidden: true` (found:
  all 3 `admin` commands, 1 `mcpcmd` command) and stub/TODO patterns (repo-wide grep found
  exactly one: `ai connect`'s API-key path is genuinely unimplemented, falls back to
  subscription sign-in — the CLI is otherwise not stubbed, confirming `docs.txt`'s own
  framing that the gap is documentation, not unfinished code).
- **V4** `00-summary.docs` — the consolidated artifact. Also found, not anticipated in
  scoping: **7 directories with zero `cobra.Command` definitions anywhere**
  (`deployui`, `envbanner`, `internal`, `projectconfig`, `projectcontext`, `state`, `ui` — 43
  files total, confirmed by direct grep) — these are support/library packages, not CLI
  surface, and are excluded from the inventory entirely rather than treated as an
  undocumented gap. This resolves `gaps/004` (`internal`'s publication status) definitively
  rather than leaving it a judgment call for Era 10.

**Headline finding:** `service` (46 commands, incl. nested `database`/`cluster`/
`backup-destination`) and `cloud` (31 commands) are the two largest command groups in the
entire CLI and have **zero** existing documentation — matches the pre-work estimate exactly.

### Era 2 — Disclosure Boundary & Templates (V5–V7) — ✅ done, verified 2026-09-17

- **V5** `DISCLOSURE.md` — the checklist, the named checkpoint-term list, and two worked
  examples (`machine drain` compliant-as-written; `state drift` shown both compliant and
  non-compliant, calibrated directly against the `docs.txt` `--wait` example).
- **V6** `templates/command-page-template.mdx` + `templates/example-machine-reboot.mdx` (the
  worked example, filled from real, source-verified `beaver machine reboot`/`reboot-impact`
  behavior in `commands/machine/maintenance.go`). Both rendered via a live `mint dev` and
  fetched over HTTP (200, correct `<title>`, components confirmed rendered rather than
  showing as literal escaped text) — caught and fixed one real bug along the way: MDX
  requires `{/* */}` comments, not HTML `<!-- -->`, which failed the build on first attempt.
- **V7** `cli/shared-flags.mdx` — **published for real**, not just planned, since Phase 2
  family pages need it to exist to link against. Content is the actual authoritative source,
  not a frequency guess: found that `--json`/`--output`/`--quiet`/`--yes`/`--wait`/
  `--timeout` are registered by one shared function, `output.RegisterFlags()`
  (`beaver-cli/output/output.go`), called by outside `commands/` entirely, so
  `commands.csv` doesn't show these flags on those commands (logged as a known, deliberate
  extraction-scope gap in `inventory/00-summary.docs` rather than silently wrong). Read
  `output.Wait`'s actual polling/timeout implementation directly to write the `--wait`
  section to the same standard the `docs.txt` conversation itself set as the bar. `mint
  broken-links` clean after publishing (one broken link found and fixed first — a literal
  placeholder link in the template, not a real page). **Re-verified 2026-09-17:** the "69
  commands" figure above was a stale hand-count (raw call-site grep gives 145, which also
  isn't the right number, since some call sites are loops covering 20+ commands each) —
  `build_summary.py` now computes the true distinct-command count live from source on every
  regeneration instead of hardcoding it (currently 196). `cli/shared-flags.mdx`'s six flag
  entries re-checked word-for-word against `output.go` source: accurate, no drift.

