## Phase 2 — Reference build-out, by family

### Era 3 — Identity, Session & Account (V8–V10) — ✅ done, verified 2026-09-17

`auth` (login/logout/whoami — currently three orphaned pages, consolidate under one family
page or cross-link tightly), `account` (has a page — verify/extend), `billing` (has a page —
verify/extend), `coupon` (no page — small, 2 files).

**Phase 2 re-verification, 2026-09-17 — gap found and closed:** neither `environment` nor
`project` was assigned to any Phase 2 era in `00-architecture.docs`'s family table — a real
planning omission, not a deliberate exclusion. Both had pre-existing pages
(`cli/environment.mdx`, `cli/project.mdx`) already wired into `docs.json` nav, but each was a
19-line stub with no Purpose/Syntax/Flags/Consequences sections and most of its flags
undocumented (`environment`: 6/7 flags missing, including `--reveal` on a command that prints
secrets; `project`: 2/3 missing, including the irreversible `delete`'s consequences going
unstated). Both rewritten to the Era 2 V6 template this pass, source-verified against
`commands/environment/*.go` and `commands/project/project.go`. See `gaps/00-index.docs` entry
012.

### Era 4 — Connect, Machine & Health (V11–V14) — ✅ done, verified 2026-09-17

`connect` (single wizard command, has a page — verify against the 23-file implementation),
`machine` (60 flag sites, largest single group by that measure, has a page — likely needs
the deepest verification pass of any "already documented" family), `doctor`, `agent`,
`health` (no page), `recover`.

### Era 5 — Deploy & Containers (V15–V18) — ✅ done, verified 2026-09-17

`deploy` (32 flag sites, single flat command, has a page), `compose`, `container`/
`containers`, `docker`, `deployment`, `deployui` (no page), `promote` (no page).

**Phase 2 re-verification, 2026-09-17:** `container.mdx` was missing `open`'s `--live` flag
— added. `container.mdx`/`containers.mdx`'s mapping in `cross_reference.py` corrected (both
now attributed to the `container` group, since `containers` is a second top-level command
literal in the same source file — content itself was already accurate, this was a
tooling/attribution fix, not a content gap). `beaver destroy` (found missing from the
inventory in the Phase 1 pass) was already correctly documented on `container.mdx` — no
content gap there, confirmed by re-reading.

### Era 6 — Infrastructure Pools (V19–V22) — ✅ done, verified 2026-09-17

`cloud` (**no page**, 29 subcommands, second-largest zero-coverage group), `scaling`,
`autoscale` (no page), `edge` (42 flag sites), `domain`, `firewall` (41 flag sites).

**Phase 2 re-verification, 2026-09-17:** `edge.mdx` was missing `firewall rule add`'s
`--name`/`--method` and `firewall rule update`'s `--conditions` and `firewall ban`'s
`--reason` — added, source-verified against `commands/edge/firewall.go`. `firewall.mdx`
(the standalone deployment-scoped family, distinct from `edge`'s Connected-App-scoped one)
was missing `rule add`'s `--method` — added.

### Era 7 — Services & Data (V23–V26) — ✅ done, verified 2026-09-17

`service` (**no page**, 37 subcommands including nested `database`/`cluster`/
`backup-destination` groups — largest undocumented surface in the whole CLI), `integration`
(no page; `integrations.mdx` exists — reconcile naming), `github`.

### Era 8 — Observability & Diagnostics (V27–V29) — ✅ done, verified 2026-09-17

`observability` (no page as a family, but its subcommands `logs`/`metrics`/`traffic`/
`latency`/`active`/`live` each have a standalone page today — decide in V27 whether to keep
them standalone or consolidate under one `observability` reference with the individual pages
as redirects/aliases), `observe`, `history`, `status`, `inspect`, `diff`.

### Era 9 — Config, State & Contracts (V30–V33) — ✅ done, verified 2026-09-17 · **highest disclosure risk**

`config` (55 flag sites, highest density in the CLI, no page despite the size), `state`/
`statecmd`, `projectconfig`, `projectcontext`, `projectcontract` (`contract.mdx`/
`validate.mdx` exist and map here — verify they don't already leak reconcile/contract
internals; if they do, this era's first job is redaction, not just completion).

**Phase 2 re-verification, 2026-09-17:** confirmed via `main.go` directly that
`projectcontract`'s commands are wired at runtime as `beaver plan`, `beaver validate`, and
`beaver config push/pull/diff/status/rollback/delete/containers` — there is no `beaver
projectcontract <verb>` invocation at all; the Go package name is internal-only. `contract.mdx`
(a 1-line-Purpose stub for a command, `beaver contract show`, that no longer exists in source
at all) had already been correctly deleted. Its replacement coverage is `plan.mdx` (accurate,
already matches `PlanCmd` source exactly) and `validate.mdx` (accurate, matches `ValidateCmd`
source exactly) for the two root commands, plus `config.mdx` for the seven nested ones —
`config.mdx` already covered `push`/`pull`/`diff`/`status`/`rollback`/`delete`/`containers`
correctly. Added to `config.mdx` this pass: the six `ConfigCmd`-level persistent flags used
by `init`/`sync` (`--strategy`/`--domain`/`--health-path`/`--compose-file`/`--project-id`/
`--port`, the last explicitly noted as informational-only per its own `--help` text), and
`bind add`/`volume add`'s flags (`--source`/`--target`/`--read-only`/`--yes-i-know`/
`--external`), previously undocumented. `health`'s `--tcp`/`--command` and `show`'s
`--effective` are genuinely reserved/not-yet-functional per their own source comments —
correctly left undocumented per Invariant 3 rather than described as working. `cross_reference.py`'s
group-to-page mapping updated to reflect the real `projectcontract` → `plan`/`validate`/`config`
relationship, closing every previously-orphaned page in this family.

### Era 10 — Admin, Preflight & Platform Ops (V34–V36) — ✅ done, verified 2026-09-17

`admin`, `preflight` (13 flag sites, no page), `mystic`, `envbanner`, `initcmd` (`init.mdx`
exists, reconcile naming), `internal` (9 files — name strongly suggests operator/CI-only;
V34's first job is deciding whether any of this belongs in public docs at all).

**Phase 2 re-verification, 2026-09-17:** `init.mdx` was an 18-line example-only stub (no
Purpose/Syntax/Consequences, missing the `--from-existing` flag entirely) despite `initcmd`
being marked resolved in Phase 1's gap 010 — "resolved" there meant the public/internal
classification question, not page completeness. Rewritten to the full template this pass,
source-verified against `commands/initcmd/init.go`.

**Admin removed, 2026-09-17 (`gaps/013`):** explicit user instruction to remove all admin
documentation. `cli/admin.mdx` deleted, removed from `docs.json`. This supersedes gap 010's
`documented-minimal` classification for `admin` — no page at all now, not even a minimal
one. `admin` reverts to `undocumented` in the regenerated inventory; see `gaps/013` before
re-creating this page.

### Era 11 — AI Surface (V37–V39) — ✅ done, verified 2026-09-17

`ai` (has a page), `alie` (has a page but 56 files/41 subcommands/22 flag sites — almost
certainly under-documented relative to size), `skillscmd` (no page), `mcpcmd` (no page —
MCP wiring is a plausible disclosure risk, verify before publishing anything about it).

**Phase 2 re-verification, 2026-09-17:** `alie.mdx` was missing the `audit` command entirely
(source: `commands/alie/audit.go`, "Show Alie's tool and action audit trail" — added with
its `--event-type`/`--limit` flags) and `sessions`' `--all` / `delete`'s `--force` flags —
all added, source-verified, two-read disclosure pass applied per this family's own elevated-
risk status (no mechanism language found or introduced). **`speccmd` was never assigned to
any era at all** in `00-architecture.docs`'s family table — a second planning omission
alongside `environment`/`project` (Era 3's note). `beaver spec` is real, visible, and
carries an explicit compatibility promise in its own source comment ("third-party editors
and Beaver Desktop should be able to find and rely on it") — `cli/spec.mdx` written this
pass and wired into `docs.json`'s Utilities group. `mcpcmd` stays excluded per gap 005's
prior resolution — re-confirmed, not re-litigated.

