## Cross-cutting risk register

| Risk | Era | Mitigation designed in |
| --- | --- | --- |
| A page accidentally documents the reconcile/contract/orchestration mechanism | 9 (mainly), all | Invariant 6 checklist applied per-page; Era 9 gets an explicit second pass before publish |
| `service`/`config` pages become unreasonably long single files | 7, 9 | V23/V30 decide per-family whether to split into sub-pages (mirrors `cli/`'s existing pattern of separate pages per concern) before writing |
| Naming mismatches between CLI groups and existing doc pages cause dead or duplicate content | 1, 12 | Era 1 inventory records every mismatch found; Era 12 is the reconciliation pass, not each family era improvising its own fix |
| A command looks implemented in `Use:`/help text but is actually a stub | 1 | V3's maturity classification requires a source spot-check, not help-text trust (Invariant 1) |
| The AI/MCP surface (`alie`, `mcpcmd`) discloses agent-tool or transport internals | 11 | Same Invariant 6 checklist, applied explicitly rather than assumed covered by the general rule |
| Docs drift again after this roadmap ships | 13 | V44–V47 is a standing process, not a cleanup; gate criterion 8 requires it be discoverable from the CLI repo itself |
